    "isNew": false,
    "codeLanguage": "javascript",
    "title": "Che cos'è JSON?",
    "descriptionContent": "Scopri i JSON e perché sono utili per gli sviluppatori front-end.",
    "shortDescriptionContent": "",
    "showInTrack": true,
    "iconBanner": null,
    "chapters": [
      {
        "id": 17523,
        "title": "Un JSON in JS",
        "type": "practiceLevel1",
        "lessons": [
          {
            "title": "Lesson #1",
            "id": 148616,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Sai già cos'è un oggetto JS. Ora scopriamo cos'è JSON. JSON sta per <strong>JavaScript Object Notation</strong>.</p><p>Nei giochi, possiamo usare questo formato di dati per memorizzare e scambiare elementi come le statistiche del giocatore, i file di salvataggio e i dati dei livelli.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #2",
            "id": 148617,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>JSON sembra una versione <em>serializzata</em> di un normale oggetto JS.</p><p>Possiamo creare <code>jsonLevelData</code> come un normale oggetto <code>{}</code>, ma racchiuso tra apici singoli <code>'</code>.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"22\" endIndex=\"23\" /><option startIndex=\"23\" endIndex=\"24\" /><option startIndex=\"24\" endIndex=\"25\" /><option startIndex=\"25\" endIndex=\"26\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" jsonLevelData = \" /><text value=\"'{}'\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\";\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Assicurati di scegliere <code>'</code>, seguito da <code>{</code> e poi <code>}</code>, <code>'</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #3",
            "id": 148618,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Un oggetto JSON contiene una raccolta di coppie chiave-valore, simile a un oggetto JS.</p><p>Tuttavia, in un JSON, dobbiamo racchiudere le chiavi tra virgolette, come <code>\"score\"</code> qui.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"41\" endIndex=\"42\" /><option startIndex=\"42\" endIndex=\"47\" /><option startIndex=\"47\" endIndex=\"48\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" jsonString = \" /><text value=\"'{&quot;player&quot;: &quot;Ranger&quot;, &quot;score&quot;: 200, &quot;alive&quot;: true }'\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\";\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Assicurati di scegliere <code>\"</code>, seguito da <code>score</code> e infine <code>\"</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #4",
            "id": 148619,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Gli oggetti JSON possono raccogliere dati statici come numeri, array, booleani o stringhe. Tuttavia, <strong>non possono</strong> contenere funzioni al loro interno.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"function(){}\" /></content></option><option startIndex=\"60\" endIndex=\"64\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" saveFile = \" /><text value=\"'{&quot;player&quot;: &quot;Ranger&quot;,&quot;score&quot;: 200,&quot;alive&quot;: true}'\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\";\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Assicurati di scegliere <code>true</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #5",
            "id": 148620,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Qual è il seguente tipo di dati?</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" player = {\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"inventory\" class=\"attr\" /><text value=\": [\" /><text value=\"&quot;potion&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;sword&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;shield&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\"],\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"health\" class=\"attr\" /><text value=\": \" /><text value=\"100\" class=\"number\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"};\" /></content></code><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">Un oggetto JS</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Un JSON</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Un oggetto JS.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #6",
            "id": 148621,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Puoi convertire un oggetto JS in JSON con il metodo <code>JSON.stringify()</code>.</p><p>Qui possiamo convertire l'oggetto JS <code>enemy</code> in una stringa JSON se usiamo <code>JSON.stringify(enemy)</code>.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"75\" endIndex=\"79\" /><option startIndex=\"80\" endIndex=\"89\" /><option startIndex=\"90\" endIndex=\"95\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" enemy = {\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"type\" class=\"attr\" /><text value=\": \" /><text value=\"&quot;Slime&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\",\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"hp\" class=\"attr\" /><text value=\": \" /><text value=\"12\" class=\"number\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"};\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(enemy);\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(\" /><text value=\"JSON\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".stringify(enemy));\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Assicurati di scegliere <code>JSON</code>, seguito da <code>stringify</code> e infine <code>enemy</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #7",
            "id": 148622,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Possiamo anche trasformare una stringa JSON in un oggetto JS con il metodo <code>JSON.parse()</code>.</p><p>Se includiamo <code>playerSave</code> tra parentesi, trasformeremo la stringa JSON in un oggetto JS.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"60\" endIndex=\"64\" /><option startIndex=\"65\" endIndex=\"70\" /><option startIndex=\"71\" endIndex=\"81\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" playerSave = \" /><text value=\"'{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Nova&quot;,&quot;level&quot;:3}'\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(\" /><text value=\"JSON\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".parse(playerSave));\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Assicurati di scegliere <code>JSON</code>, seguito da <code>parse</code> e infine <code>playerSave</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #8",
            "id": 148623,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Come possiamo convertire un oggetto JS in una stringa JSON?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">Con <code>JSON.stringify</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Con <code>JSON.parse</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Con <code>JSON.stringify</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #9",
            "id": 148624,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Cosa visualizzerà la console?</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" gameState = {\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"score\" class=\"attr\" /><text value=\": \" /><text value=\"13\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\",\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"paused\" class=\"attr\" /><text value=\": \" /><text value=\"false\" class=\"literal\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"};\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(\" /><text value=\"JSON\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".stringify(gameState));\" /></content></code><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\"><code>{\"score\": 13, \"paused\": false}</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\"><code>{score: 13, paused : false}</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\"><code>{\"score\": 13, \"paused\": false}</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #10",
            "id": 148625,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Completa il seguente JSON.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"18\" endIndex=\"19\" /><option startIndex=\"20\" endIndex=\"21\" /><option startIndex=\"25\" endIndex=\"26\" /><option startIndex=\"56\" endIndex=\"57\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" levelInfo = \" /><text value=\"'{&quot;name&quot;: &quot;Forest-1&quot;, &quot;enemies&quot;: 123 }'\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\";\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Assicurati di scegliere <code>'</code>, seguito da <code>\"</code> e poi <code>\"</code>, <code>'</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #11",
            "id": 148626,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>*<em>Analizza</em> la stringa JSON <code>saveData</code> in modo da visualizzare un oggetto JS nell'output della console.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"validatedInput\" startIndex=\"88\" endIndex=\"93\" isDefault=\"true\" /></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" saveData = \" /><text value=\"'{&quot;player&quot;: &quot;Nova&quot;, &quot;checkpoint&quot;:&quot;Cave&quot;}'\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" parsedSaveData = \" /><text value=\"JSON\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".parse(saveData);\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(parsedSaveData);\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Assicurati di digitare <code>parse</code>.</p></body></html>"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}